-- title:
--   Flatness at p of the Taylor–Wiles level Galois representation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, and let $p$ be a prime lying in its maximal ideal. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over the residue field $k$ of $\mathcal{O}$, absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to $\overline{k}$ has no Galois-stable submodule other than $0$ and the whole space. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $N \neq 0$ an integer all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, and $r \neq 0$ a prime not dividing $N$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q \mid N$ prime, $q \notin S$), such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $P$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct nonzero primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, let $\pi_i \colon (\mathbb{Z}/q_i)^{\times} \to \mathbb{Z}/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ (multiplicatively written) be homomorphisms, and let $\alpha \colon \{1,\dots,t\} \to k$. Write $L = N\,(\prod_i q_i)\, r$ for `level N r qv` and $H_Q$ for the subgroup `HQ N r qv p πΔ` of $(\mathbb{Z}/L)^{\times}$ cut out by $H_r$ and the kernel of $(\pi_i)_i$. Assume the Hecke generators at this level commute pairwise (`OpComm`) and commute with the diamond operators (`DiaComm`), and let $T_Q$ denote the resulting ring `HeckeRing`, the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}}$ of the associated module generated by the Hecke generators. Assume $T_Q$ is local, Noetherian and adically complete, that $\mathcal{O} \to T_Q$ is a local homomorphism, that $T_Q$ is a finite $\mathcal{O}$-module, and that $\mathcal{O} \to T_Q \to T_Q/\mathfrak{m}_{T_Q}$ is surjective. Let $\rho'$ be an adically continuous Galois representation on a free $T_Q$-module of rank two such that for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ (in the sense above) one has $\operatorname{tr}\rho'(\sigma) = T_\ell \in T_Q$, and such that the residual representation of $\rho'$ is isomorphic, as a Galois representation, to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Assume finally $p \nmid L$. Then $\rho'$ is flat at $p$: the residue field of $T_Q$ is finite, and for every ideal $I$ of $T_Q$ with $T_Q/I$ finite there exist a commutative ring $H$ carrying a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over the subring $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \subset \mathbb{Q}$ of rationals with denominator prime to $p$, finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-module, and a bijection $e$ from the convolution group of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra homomorphisms $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto $\rho'.V/(I \cdot \rho'.V)$ which is additive and Galois-equivariant, in the sense that $e(g) = \sigma \cdot e(f)$ whenever $g = \sigma \circ f$ pointwise, the action on the quotient being the one induced by $\rho'(\sigma)$.
--
--   This is the local condition at $p$ (Wiles's "flat" type) satisfied by the modular deformation on the branch of the Taylor–Wiles argument in which $p$ does not divide the level $N q_1 \cdots q_t r$: each finite torsion quotient of the representation is realised as the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of a finite flat commutative group scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. It feeds the construction of the modular Galois representation over the Taylor–Wiles level Hecke ring together with its local behaviour, used in [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_flat`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_flat).
